{
    "background_story": "Angie was a talented baker who had a passion for creating the perfect loaf of bread. Growing up in a small village, she learned the art of bread-making from her grandmother, who owned a quaint bakery. Angie's love for bread was more than just a hobby - it was a way to connect with her community. She spent years perfecting her recipe, experimenting with different flours and techniques. Her bakery, 'Angie's Loaves,' quickly became a staple in the village, with locals and tourists alike flocking to taste her mouthwatering creations. From crusty baguettes to hearty sourdough, Angie's loaves were always made with love and care. Her dedication to her craft earned her the title of 'Village Baker,' and her bakery remained a cozy gathering place for the community.",
